                "claim": "Worktree no longer uses g.observer(); it builds its own gitprov.Observer inline. The observer() helper still exists and is used only by Locate, so two construction sites of the same Observer now exist and can drift (e.g. a future change to Environ or Run wiring in one place but not the other). Worktree's inline observer also duplicates the ambient/Run wiring that observer() encapsulates.",
