                "claim": "answered() relies on ExitCode() \u003e= 0 to mean 'ran to an exit status', but the unit test constructs a zero-value exec.ExitError for the 'killed by a signal' case; the relationship between ExitError with nil ProcessState (ExitCode returns -1) and the real signal case is implicit and only explained by the test name. A short comment in answered noting that ExitCode is -1 for signal termination would make the intent verifiable.",
                "proof_refs": [
