              "engine/review/gitexec/gitexec.go: Worktree now returns an error instead of 'taken' when git was never asked, or when the runner error is a *failure (git did not start, was killed by a signal, or the deadline passed). An exit status with a live context still counts as git's answer. The deadline check uses ctx.Err() before cancel, and an ExitError with a nil ProcessState reports an exit code of -1, so a signal kill is classified as no answer.",
